.th TLIMIT II 4/2/77
.sh NAME
tlimit \*- set process time limit
.sh SYNOPSIS
(tlimit = 39.; not in assembler)
.br
(new time limit, in seconds, in r0)
.br
.ft B
sys tlimit
.br
.ft R
(seconds remaining, to old limit, in r0)
.s3
.ft B
tlimit(nsec);
.ft R
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Tlimit
sets a limit on the sum of system and user times.
On expiration of the limit a signal 16 is generated.
A limit of zero will disable time limit checking.
The interval is passed to children across forks.
.it Tlimit
returns a word (in r0) containing the seconds remaining to expiration
of the previous time limit.
.sh "SEE ALSO"
signal (II)
.sh DIAGNOSTICS
